message.content:
To fix the bug where supplementary Unicode characters are encoded twice (once correctly and once as an invalid surrogate), the loop must correctly handle code points that span two characters (surrogate pairs) by incrementing the index by the number of characters each code point occupies. This prevents processing individual surrogates as separate code points.

```java
    private static void appendToAscii(String s, boolean spaceAsPlus, StringBuilder sb) throws UnsupportedEncodingException {
        // minimal normalization of Unicode -> Ascii, and space normal. Existing escapes are left as-is.
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); ) {
            int c = s.codePointAt(i);
            if (c == ' ') {
                sb.append(spaceAsPlus ? '+' : "%20");
            } else if (c > 127) { // out of ascii range
                sb.append(URLEncoder.encode(new String(Character.toChars(c)), UTF_8.name()));
                // ^^ is a bit heavy-handed - if perf critical, we could optimize
            } else {
                sb.append((char) c);
            }
            i += Character.charCount(c); // correctly advance over surrogate pairs
        }
